{#
	A value that names another record, drawn as a way to get there (XIV-42).

	The caller keeps its own idea of what an empty value looks like — a dash on a
	record page, nothing in a list — and hands in the text it already resolved.
	All this decides is whether that text is a link.

	Nothing here asks what *kind* of field it is holding. `record_link()` asks the
	field type, which either has an answer or has not, and a stale reference or
	one the reader may not open answers null and stays text (§7.6, §8.4).
#}
{% macro linked(field, raw, shown) %}
	{%- set link = record_link(field, raw) -%}
	{%- if link is not null -%}
		<a href="{{ path('module_show', {module: link.module, id: link.id}) }}">{{ shown }}</a>
	{%- else -%}
		{{- shown -}}
	{%- endif -%}
{% endmacro %}
